WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.435
-The President has been accused

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:04.203
of working for
a foreign government

00:00:04.203 --> 00:00:06.272
while our own government
remains shut down.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:09.308
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.308 --> 00:00:13.579
♪♪

00:00:13.579 --> 00:00:15.581
The government shutdown
is now the longest in history,

00:00:15.581 --> 00:00:17.016
with no end in sight.

00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:19.585
In fact, today the President
stopped by reporters

00:00:19.585 --> 00:00:22.489
to let them know he was
carrying on with other business,

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:24.557
like a speech
to a group of farmers.

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:27.226
-I'll be going to New Orleans
right now.

00:00:27.226 --> 00:00:30.663
I'm going to be speaking
in front of our great farmers.

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:32.731
-Okay, got it.
He's on his way to New Orleans.

00:00:32.731 --> 00:00:35.235
Or at least I think he is,
because this morning

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:37.837
one of Trump's
other personalities tweeted,

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:41.074
"Getting ready to address the
farm convention in Nashville."

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:43.876
Hey, at least
it started with an "N."

00:00:43.876 --> 00:00:47.313
And in fairness to Trump,
it was only his fourth guess.

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:49.382
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:52.318
So while Trump
was off to New Orleans,

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:54.720
or as he calls it,
the home of country music,

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.555
the effects of the shutdown
were having

00:00:56.555 --> 00:00:58.691
very real consequences
for millions of people.

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:00.794
For example, over the weekend,
federal employees

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:02.595
showed up to food banks
in the hundreds.

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:05.197
But that's not the food
Trump was concerned with today.

00:01:05.197 --> 00:01:07.867
He was much more concerned
with the food he'll be serving

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.569
at the White House
for a ceremony

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:12.038
with the college-football
championship team from Clemson,

00:01:12.038 --> 00:01:14.007
as he explained to reporters.

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:17.577
-The Clemson championship team,
the national championship team,

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:18.845
will be coming tonight.

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:21.648
It will be exciting.
Very great team.

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:24.917
An unbelievable team.
They'll be coming tonight.

00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:28.153
And I think we're going to serve
McDonald's, Wendy's,

00:01:28.153 --> 00:01:30.156
and Burger Kings
with some pizza.

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:32.325
I really mean it.
It will be interesting.

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:34.827
And I would think
that's their favorite food.

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:38.865
-No, dude, I think
that's your favorite food.

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:41.033
He thinks he's being so sly.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:43.669
"Normally, I would have a salad
for dinner on Monday,

00:01:43.669 --> 00:01:47.907
but they told me
they only eat every fast food."

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:49.675
Also, can we go back to this?

00:01:49.675 --> 00:01:53.680
-McDonald's, Wendy's, and
Burger Kings with some pizza.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:58.585
-Why does he say "Burger Kings,"
plural?

00:01:58.585 --> 00:02:02.088
Does he think
there's more than one?

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:04.891
"We will be having
all of the Burger Kings

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:08.595
over to the White House
for a summit on trade."

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:10.096
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:11.931
[ Applause ]

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:15.368
I think...

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:18.304
I think it's safe to say
that had he lost the election,

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:20.540
the Burger Kings would have been
the name of the food show

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.442
Trump hosted with Guy Fieri.

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:23.942
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.942 --> 00:02:25.845
Now, it is entirely possible
that Trump thought

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:27.513
shutting down the government
would make

00:02:27.513 --> 00:02:29.115
the Russia investigation
just go away.

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:30.783
I'm sure his lawyers
told him that.

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:32.652
"You can't be arrested
by the government

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:35.054
if there is no government!"

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:37.689
But as we found out on Friday,
that is very much not the case.

00:02:37.689 --> 00:02:40.193
In fact, we got one of
the biggest blockbusters yet.

00:02:40.193 --> 00:02:42.561
-Breaking news tonight
from "The New York Times."

00:02:42.561 --> 00:02:45.164
The FBI opened an inquiry
into whether President Trump

00:02:45.164 --> 00:02:48.468
was secretly working
on behalf of Russia.

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:50.369
In the days after
President Trump fired

00:02:50.369 --> 00:02:53.338
James B. Comey as FBI director,

00:02:53.338 --> 00:02:54.841
law-enforcement officials

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:57.644
became so concerned
by the President's behavior

00:02:57.644 --> 00:03:01.080
that they began investigating
whether he had been working

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:05.618
on behalf of Russia
against American interests.

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:08.354
-Wow.
The FBI was investigating

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:10.790
whether Trump was working
for the Russians.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.458
I mean, what tipped them off?

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:14.860
Was it Trump's secret
meeting with the Russians
in the Oval Office,

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.729
his son's secret meeting
with Russians in Trump Tower,

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:18.665
his lawyer's secret deal to
build a Trump Tower in Moscow,

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:20.432
Jeff Session's secret meeting
with the Russian ambassador,

00:03:20.432 --> 00:03:22.100
Jared Kushner's secret
back channel with the Kremlin,

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:23.836
Michael Flynn's secret
back channel with the Kremlin,

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:25.605
Erik Prince's secret
back channel with the Kremlin,

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:27.473
Paul Manafort sharing secret
polling data with the Russians,

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:29.442
his foreign policy
advisor's secret meeting
with the Russians,

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:30.976
the Russian hackers
who helped Trump win,

00:03:30.976 --> 00:03:32.812
Trump asking the Russian hackers
to help him win,

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:35.982
or Vladimir Putin's smile
every time he sees Trump?

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:38.217
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:40.619
Look at that.

00:03:40.619 --> 00:03:44.790
That's the smile Putin gives
when someone says,

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:46.793
"We have captured James Bond."

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:49.595
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.595 --> 00:03:52.197
Trump has also met privately
with Putin multiple times,

00:03:52.197 --> 00:03:54.667
and over the weekend,
"The Washington Post" reported

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:57.269
that Trump has gone to
extraordinary lengths to conceal

00:03:57.269 --> 00:03:58.971
details of his conversations
with Putin,

00:03:58.971 --> 00:04:00.506
including,
on at least one occasion,

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:03.008
taking possession of the notes
of his own interpreter.

00:04:03.008 --> 00:04:05.611
Now, we don't know what
Trump did with those notes,

00:04:05.611 --> 00:04:07.747
but we do know
that in her tell-all book,

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:10.048
former Trump aide Omarosa said
she saw Trump

00:04:10.048 --> 00:04:12.718
trying to destroy evidence
by eating a piece of paper

00:04:12.718 --> 00:04:14.554
in the Oval Office.

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:17.690
And if you forgot
that the President

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:20.359
was accused of eating paper
by his own aide,

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:23.062
take note of the fact that we
are living through a presidency

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:27.934
where that insane fact might
actually qualify as forgettable.

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:31.036
For every other president
before him, eating paper

00:04:31.036 --> 00:04:33.472
would be number one on the list

00:04:33.472 --> 00:04:35.374
of craziest [bleep] things,
but...

00:04:35.374 --> 00:04:37.477
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:44.350
But for Trash Can Jones
over here,

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:49.455
it doesn't even crack
the top 100.

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:52.858
We for real have a president
who may one day say,

00:04:52.858 --> 00:04:55.294
"If you want my notes,
you'll need a search warrant...

00:04:55.294 --> 00:04:57.730
for my belly."

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:00.299
And, of course,
Trump wants to keep the details

00:05:00.299 --> 00:05:02.134
of his conversation
with Putin secret.

00:05:02.134 --> 00:05:04.503
Every time we find out
about a private conversation

00:05:04.503 --> 00:05:07.239
he had with Putin, it turns out
he said something suspicious.

00:05:07.239 --> 00:05:09.175
Like when Putin
won a rigged election

00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:11.577
and Trump's aides wrote
in his briefings in all caps,

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:14.413
"DO NOT CONGRATULATE,"
and then Trump said this.

00:05:14.413 --> 00:05:17.416
-I had a call
with President Putin

00:05:17.416 --> 00:05:20.586
and congratulated him
on the victory.

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:22.120
-Now, in fairness to Trump,

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:25.091
he would have read the briefing,
but he was hungry.

00:05:25.091 --> 00:05:27.059
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.059 --> 00:05:28.861
So the President
was being investigated

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:30.896
for possibly working
for a foreign government

00:05:30.896 --> 00:05:33.699
and at the same time
he was shutting down
our own government.

00:05:33.699 --> 00:05:36.102
If it feels to you like our
political system is in chaos

00:05:36.102 --> 00:05:37.436
right now, you're not alone.

00:05:37.436 --> 00:05:39.538
The only one who disagrees
is Trump himself,

00:05:39.538 --> 00:05:42.008
and he made that clear
in a tweet over the weekend.

00:05:42.008 --> 00:05:43.842
-"I just watched a fake reporter

00:05:43.842 --> 00:05:45.744
from the Amazon
'Washington Post'

00:05:45.744 --> 00:05:48.180
say the White House is chaotic.

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:50.649
There does not seem to be
a strategy for this shutdown.

00:05:50.649 --> 00:05:52.250
There is no plan.

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:55.555
The fakes always like
talking chaos. There is none.

00:05:55.555 --> 00:05:59.558
In fact, there's almost nobody
in the White House but me."

00:05:59.558 --> 00:06:01.293
-What?!

00:06:01.293 --> 00:06:03.195
Nothing is more chaotic

00:06:03.195 --> 00:06:08.634
than a huge building
with only one person working.

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:11.270
That's why RadioShack
went out of business.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:12.805
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:15.307
So Trump says he's all alone
in the White House,

00:06:15.307 --> 00:06:18.477
which leaves him plenty of time
to do important president stuff,

00:06:18.477 --> 00:06:21.046
like call into Fox News
and scream a lot.

00:06:21.046 --> 00:06:22.948
And that's what he did
on Saturday.

00:06:22.948 --> 00:06:25.718
Fox host Jeanine Pirro started
by asking about the shutdown,

00:06:25.718 --> 00:06:27.720
and right off the bat,
Trump told an obvious lie.

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.856
-You're sitting there
waiting for a deal.

00:06:29.856 --> 00:06:34.059
The Democrats are not
sitting with you.

00:06:34.059 --> 00:06:38.897
If this isn't an emergency,
I don't know what is.

00:06:38.897 --> 00:06:42.268
-Well, I haven't actually left
the White House in months.

00:06:42.268 --> 00:06:43.636
-What?!

00:06:43.636 --> 00:06:46.372
We've seen you leave
the White House repeatedly.

00:06:46.372 --> 00:06:48.508
Last week, you went
to the southern border,

00:06:48.508 --> 00:06:51.243
and in December you visited
the troops in Iraq, remember?

00:06:51.243 --> 00:06:53.513
You were wearing one of those
oversized jackets

00:06:53.513 --> 00:06:55.615
you borrowed from Tom Brady?

00:06:55.615 --> 00:06:57.016
[ Laughter ]

00:06:57.016 --> 00:06:58.984
Why is your coat so big?

00:06:58.984 --> 00:07:02.388
Are you sneaking immigrants
over the border?

00:07:02.388 --> 00:07:04.823
[ Laughter ]

00:07:04.823 --> 00:07:10.596
"We're almost --
We're almost back on the plane."

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:13.666
So, Trump claimed he hadn't left
the White House in months,

00:07:13.666 --> 00:07:15.134
which led Pirro to grill him

00:07:15.134 --> 00:07:18.371
with a series of super-tough
follow-up questions.

00:07:18.371 --> 00:07:21.040
-Mr. President, when
are you gonna get out
of the White House?

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:25.344
I mean, Washington after a while
gets very depressing.

00:07:25.344 --> 00:07:26.845
-Well, I love it.

00:07:26.845 --> 00:07:29.315
-Mr. President, I really hope
you get out of the White House.

00:07:29.315 --> 00:07:32.685
I really do.
I think you deserve a vacation.

00:07:32.685 --> 00:07:35.955
-Wow, Jeanine. That's a real
hard-hitting question.

00:07:35.955 --> 00:07:37.490
Just because you're shouting,

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:39.191
it doesn't mean
you're grilling him.

00:07:39.191 --> 00:07:41.727
"You deserve a vacation!
And I'll tell you another thing!

00:07:41.727 --> 00:07:45.131
You're a handsome good boy!
And your skin's a normal color!"

00:07:45.131 --> 00:07:47.700
[ Laughter ]

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:51.537
Then Pirro finally got to
the news of the weekend --

00:07:51.537 --> 00:07:54.306
the FBI's investigation
into Trump.

00:07:54.306 --> 00:07:57.376
She asked Trump point-blank if
he had ever worked for Russia.

00:07:57.376 --> 00:08:00.213
And, now, any normal person
in this situation would say,

00:08:00.213 --> 00:08:01.781
"No, of course not.
That's insane."

00:08:01.781 --> 00:08:03.749
That is not how Trump responded.

00:08:03.749 --> 00:08:06.151
His entire uninterrupted answer
to that question

00:08:06.151 --> 00:08:08.087
took almost two minutes.

00:08:08.087 --> 00:08:10.556
-Are you now or have you ever
worked for Russia,

00:08:10.556 --> 00:08:11.957
Mr. President?

00:08:11.957 --> 00:08:15.460
-I think it's the most insulting
thing I've ever been asked.

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:19.231
I think it's the most insulting
article I've ever had written.

00:08:19.231 --> 00:08:23.435
You know, I fired James Comey.
I call him Lyin' James Comey.

00:08:23.435 --> 00:08:26.706
Andrew McCabe, Peter Strzok,
his lover, Lisa Page.

00:08:26.706 --> 00:08:28.274
They did it.

00:08:28.274 --> 00:08:31.310
I've been tougher on Russia
than anybody else, any other --

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:33.312
probably any other president,
period.

00:08:33.312 --> 00:08:34.947
I think it was a great insult,

00:08:34.947 --> 00:08:37.649
and "The New York Times"
is a disaster as a paper.

00:08:37.649 --> 00:08:39.918
They've gone so far that people

00:08:39.918 --> 00:08:42.989
that were necessary believers
are now big believers,

00:08:42.989 --> 00:08:44.924
because they said that was
a step too far.

00:08:44.924 --> 00:08:47.126
They really are a disaster
of a newspaper.

00:08:47.126 --> 00:08:50.830
-Not once in that entire answer
did he say the word "no."

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:53.699
I mean, that's like
if your wife asks you,

00:08:53.699 --> 00:08:55.534
"Are you sleeping with Susan?"

00:08:55.534 --> 00:08:56.935
And you said...

00:08:56.935 --> 00:09:00.238
-I think it's the most insulting
thing I've ever been asked.

00:09:00.238 --> 00:09:02.308
-So, after dodging
the question on Saturday,

00:09:02.308 --> 00:09:04.310
Trump tried to rectify
the situation today

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:06.145
by stopping by
the throng of reporters

00:09:06.145 --> 00:09:07.580
gathered on the White House lawn

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:10.282
for his usual
chopper-adjacent Q&amp;A,

00:09:10.282 --> 00:09:11.984
and they asked Trump
for a second time

00:09:11.984 --> 00:09:13.653
whether he had ever worked
for Russia.

00:09:13.653 --> 00:09:15.554
-I never worked for Russia,

00:09:15.554 --> 00:09:17.489
and you know that answer
better than anybody.

00:09:17.489 --> 00:09:18.957
I never worked for Russia.

00:09:18.957 --> 00:09:20.926
Not only did I never work
for Russia,

00:09:20.926 --> 00:09:24.296
I think it's a disgrace
that you even ask that question.

00:09:24.296 --> 00:09:26.565
Because it's
a whole, big fat hoax.

00:09:26.565 --> 00:09:28.000
-First of all, why does Trump

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.336
always choose venues
where he has to shout?

00:09:30.336 --> 00:09:33.806
He only does interviews on the
phone or next to a helicopter.

00:09:33.806 --> 00:09:35.474
If the news
gets any worse for him,

00:09:35.474 --> 00:09:38.043
he's going to do his next
press conference on speakerphone

00:09:38.043 --> 00:09:41.247
from a wind tunnel
at a performance of
the musical "Stomp."

00:09:41.247 --> 00:09:43.549
[ Laughter ]

00:09:43.549 --> 00:09:45.318
Can we go back to this
real quick?

00:09:45.318 --> 00:09:46.786
-It's a whole, big fat hoax.

00:09:46.786 --> 00:09:48.654
-Yeah, that's right.
It's a big, fat hoax.

00:09:48.654 --> 00:09:50.455
You know, a hoax
that only eats...

00:09:50.455 --> 00:09:53.658
-McDonald's, Wendy's, and
Burger Kings with some pizza.

00:09:53.658 --> 00:09:55.561
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:09:55.561 --> 00:09:58.064
♪♪

